Regression: "trust proxy" setting not inherited by mounted app

Bisect says this broke in 566720be15 (between 3.6.0 and 3.7.0) when some new capabilitites were added to `trust proxy`.

``` js
var express = require('express');
var app = express();

app.set('trust proxy', true);
app.set('foobarquux', true);

var subApp = express()
    .get('/', function (req, res) {
        res.send({ip: req.ip, foobarquux: subApp.get('foobarquux'), trust: subApp.get('trust proxy')});
    });

app.use('/', subApp);

app.listen(1337);
```

Before that commit, the above server returned:

``` json
{
  "ip": "127.0.0.1",
  "foobarquux": true,
  "trust": true
}
```

And after:

``` json
{
  "ip": "127.0.0.1",
  "foobarquux": true,
  "trust": false
}
```

As the `foobarquux` setting demonstrates, settings are clearly supposed to be inherited.

